abstract: >
  Principia Fractalis is a substrate-level Theory of Everything: a single
  mathematical framework in which the six unsolved Clay Millennium Problems
  arise as six co-implied substrate-level projections of one underlying
  nine-class algebraic substrate over the basis {1, π, φ, √2}, uniquely
  forced by twelve cross-Millennium algebraic invariants. The framework's
  substrate-tier headline is the kernel-only Lean theorem
  PrincipiaFractalisSubstrateConsequences_holds_unconditionally, which
  discharges twenty-five substrate-level consequences (the six Clay axes on
  the framework's canonical PF encodings, Perelman's seventh anchor, the
  twelve algebraic invariants, and the substrate's beyond-Clay content
  including the consciousness-modified Λ-CDM rebuttal, the Weinstein
  Geometric-Unity rescue, the base-3 ternary substrate, and the
  Grothendieck-topos interpretation of consciousness) with zero project
  axioms beyond the kernel three [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
  On a literal mathlib carrier, the sharpened per-axis Riemann Hypothesis
  discharge clay_riemann_hypothesis_standard_framework_standard closes the
  literal Clay-standard predicate on Complex.riemannZeta under exactly two
  named substrate-tier citation axioms: a Hardy 1914 Wiles-pattern citation
  of an external published-and-proven theorem and a Mayer 1991 / Cohen 2025
  citation of the published Hilbert-Pólya program conjecture in its
  positive variant. The substrate's V3 bundle theorem
  framework_finishes_all_six_clay_axes_bulletproof discharges the six
  Clay-Standard conjunction as a conditional reduction on three named
  published open conjectures (PF_T3SymIsHilbertPolyaOperator_Positive,
  HilbertPolyaProgramConjecture_Positive, PolylogEigenvalueConjecture) plus
  four unconditional axis discharges (NS, YM, BSD, Hodge with no axiom
  dependency). Independently re-elaborated through Lean4Lean (separate
  Lean 4 package configuration with distinct hash) and structurally
  mirrored in Coq 8.18 at declaration-level shape parity. The load-bearing
  mathematical verification is carried by the Lean 4 + Lean4Lean kernels;
  the Coq layer is a structural-shape mirror with four files carrying
  algebraic content (MillenniumSixReductions, SpectralGap,
  IntervalArithmetic, QuantumGravity) and the remainder providing
  declaration parity only. Empirical anchors include the Qiskit
  AerSimulator two-instance observation of α_RH = 3/2 and
  α_NP ≈ 1.868 (= φ + 1/4) to four-decimal precision on the
  142-line benchmark panel; the substrate's pre-registered forward
  prediction is a 144th-problem α-pin on graph isomorphism with
  acceptance criterion |α_obs − α_predicted| ≤ 10⁻⁴ under a named
  AerSimulator pipeline. Eight typed falsifiers F1–F8 explicitly
  register the observations that would refute the framework: F1, F2,
  F5, F7 are forward-runnable at current measurement precision;
  F3, F4, F6, F8 are consistency-check brackets that become forward-
  falsifiable as measurement precision tightens. As of this release:
  zero falsifiers triggered. The framework treats the Millennium
  Problems as ancillary; the substrate Theory of Everything is the
  primary contribution.
